 </programlisting>
     <para>This final group is used to perform what may be called=20
     <quote>managing the discourse</quote>: providing reference points to h=
elp the listener understand the flow from one sentence to the next.</para>
     <para>Other English equivalents of=20
     <quote>ta'onai</quote>are=20
     <quote>anyway</quote>,=20
     <quote>anyhow</quote>,=20
     <quote>in any case</quote>,=20
     <quote>in any event</quote>,=20
     <quote>as I was saying</quote>, and=20
     <quote>continuing</quote>.</para>
     <para>The scale of=20
     <quote>ra'u</quote>has to do with the importance of the point being, o=
r about to be, expressed:=20
+<!-- ^^   ra'u, 319; scale of importance, 320 -->
+<indexterm><primary>ra'u</primary></indexterm>
     <quote>ra'u</quote>is the most important point,=20
