     <quote>attitudinal indicators</quote>which specifically covers this ty=
pe of commentary on spoken statements. They are both written and spoken, bu=
t require no specific intonation or gestures. Grammatically they are very s=
imple: one or more attitudinals at the beginning of a bridi apply to the en=
tire bridi; anywhere else in the bridi they apply to the word immediately t=
o the left. For example:</para>
